                                Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement (1987). The
                                corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card records
                                the following information, which was deemed unsatisfactory for an
                                attribution: 'A richly illuminated leaf of a gradual, which, from a
                                memorandum on the verso, and the arms of Burgundy impaled with those
                                of France and England appearing upon it, may be presumed to have
                                belonged to a volume given to the Grey Friars of Greenwich by
                                <persName>Margaret of York, Duchess of Burgundy</persName>'. 'There
                                was a Booke called A graile given vnto the graie observant friers of
                                Greenwich by Margaret duchess of Bourgouine sister unto K: Edward
